<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Ahmad Shah Qajar</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1898–1930</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Ahmad Shah <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/qajar-dynasty">Qajar</a> was the last shah of the Qajar dynasty of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iran">Iran</a>, coming to the throne as a boy in 1909 after his father was deposed in the Constitutional Revolution. His weak reign saw foreign occupation during the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/first-world-war">First World War</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/reza-shah">Reza Khan</a>'s coup of 1921. While he was in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/europe">Europe</a>, the Majlis deposed him in 1925 and made Reza Khan shah.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/ahmad-shah-qajar.jpg" alt="Ahmad Shah Qajar" width="320" height="457" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Bain News Service · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:AhmadShahQajar2.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
